      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8cefaa1b",
      "@type": "VisualMaterial",
      "instance_name": "human_body",
      "label": "emaciated human bodies",
      "description": "Multiple bodies of severely malnourished individuals, likely Holocaust victims, are depicted. One body is suspended upside down by its feet from a wooden structure, with its head and upper torso visible. Another body lies partially covered by a blanket, with its face visible and showing extreme emaciation. Additional bodies are visible in the background, lying on the ground. The bodies are in a state of extreme suffering and death, with visible signs of starvation and trauma.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6cad026a",
      "@type": "Scene",
      "instance_name": "suffering_victims_scene",
      "label": "scene of emaciated victims in extreme suffering",
      "description": "The scene depicts multiple emaciated human bodies in a state of extreme suffering and death, likely Holocaust victims. One body is suspended upside down by its feet from a wooden structure, with its head and upper torso visible. Another body lies partially covered by a blanket, with its face visible and showing extreme emaciation. Additional bodies are visible in the background, lying on the ground. The bodies are arranged in a grim, chaotic composition, conveying a sense of horror and despair. The spatial arrangement suggests a location of mass suffering, possibly a camp or execution site. The scene is dominated by the visual elements of starvation, trauma, and death.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_82018af4",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "historical_event_holocaust",
      "label": "Holocaust",
      "description": "The Holocaust was the systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. The image depicts emaciated victims, likely from concentration camps, and is a direct reference to this genocide. Understanding the Holocaust is essential to comprehend the gravity of the suffering shown and the ethical weight of using such imagery in a meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ba6363d8",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "holocaust_minimization_theme",
      "label": "Holocaust Minimization Theme",
      "description": "This refers to the tendency to downplay, trivialize, or distort the historical reality of the Holocaust, often by reducing its horror to a metaphor for other struggles. The meme’s text 'this project is tough but it will save the world' juxtaposed with the image of Holocaust victims is an example of this theme, as it attempts to equate extreme historical suffering with a modern motivational cliché, thereby minimizing the atrocity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e67e334e",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "motivational_cliché",
      "label": "Motivational Cliché",
      "description": "The phrase 'this project is tough but it will save the world' is a common motivational trope used to justify difficult or arduous tasks by framing them as noble or world-saving. This cliché is often used in modern contexts to inspire perseverance, but when paired with imagery of genocide, it becomes exploitative and disrespectful.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d1bde407",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "exploitative_memes",
      "label": "Exploitative Memes",
      "description": "Exploitative memes use disturbing or traumatic imagery to evoke emotional responses or to justify a particular viewpoint, often by reducing the gravity of the original context. This meme uses the Holocaust imagery to frame a modern project as noble, which is exploitative because it commodifies human suffering for motivational purposes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_18d4635c",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "desensitization_to_trauma",
      "label": "Desensitization to Trauma",
      "description": "This refers to the psychological process of becoming less emotionally affected by traumatic events through repeated exposure or by using them as metaphors. The meme risks desensitizing viewers to the horror of the Holocaust by normalizing its imagery in a motivational context, potentially reducing the emotional and moral weight of historical atrocity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d90320b3",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "despair",
      "label": "despairing emotion",
      "description": "The emaciated faces and bodies of the victims, particularly the one suspended upside down with a vacant, hollow gaze and the one partially covered with a blanket showing extreme starvation and trauma, express profound despair. Their physical state and the chaotic, grim scene convey utter hopelessness and the finality of death or suffering.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c96cbc2e",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "Suffering victims are mapped onto a 'tough project'",
      "description": "The text 'this project is tough but it will save the world' is juxtaposed with the visual of emaciated, dying victims. The mapping equates the extreme suffering and death of the victims with the difficulty of a project, implying that the project's hardship is comparable to or justified by the victims' suffering. This is an analogical mapping where the visual material (suffering victims) is mapped onto the textual concept (a tough project).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2ebaa48d",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material as the subject of the motivational claim",
      "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the text 'this project is tough but it will save the world', which frames the user as the one undertaking the 'tough project'. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the motivational text creates an implicit identification with the speaker or doer of the project, making the user the projected subject of the statement. The user is projected onto the textual material to identify with the 'project' being described.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e2df0aa2",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme uses the image of Holocaust victims in extreme suffering to justify or frame a difficult project as noble or necessary, which can be seen as exploitative and disrespectful to the victims. The intent is to evoke a sense of urgency or moral justification for a project by invoking the gravity of historical atrocity, potentially normalizing or minimizing the horror of the depicted event. The overall intent is harmful as it risks desensitizing viewers to the gravity of historical trauma and may be used to justify or legitimize difficult or ethically ambiguous projects by association with suffering.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9cf47134",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who engage with internet memes, particularly those who appreciate or use motivational clichés to frame difficult tasks as noble or world-saving. This audience may include young adults and professionals who use such phrases to justify personal or organizational challenges, often in contexts of work, entrepreneurship, or activism. The meme is designed to resonate with those who are familiar with the visual language of internet culture and who may be seeking emotional or moral justification for arduous projects, potentially without fully considering the ethical implications of using Holocaust imagery. The audience is likely to be those who are desensitized to historical trauma or who are unaware of the exploitative nature of the meme, making it accessible and shareable within online communities that value 'grit' or 'sacrifice' as virtues.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_51aae241"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
  ]
